# K03 RECEIVE-OUTPUT (Codex K03-RECEIVE-OUTPUT-20261007-23; LMX_blog/q/q53.md:95-97; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# #construction, #dynamic): a computed output -- a receiver's, merge's, a computed number declaration's -- at a named
# Structure's top level is no field of it, stored at its own receiver occurrence, produced when control reaches it.
# Every computed candidate of a number declaration, not only a call: `int: j i` (a name) and `int: k i + 1` (an
# expression) are computed outputs of Host like `int: i getValue()`, each read by Host's later statements.  Exit 7;
# 81 if a candidate was not computed when Host ran.
fn: getValue () int
    return: 4
end: getValue
Out:
    int: a 0
    int: b 0
end: Out
Host:
    int: i getValue()
    int: j i
    int: k i + 1
    Out\a: j
    Out\b: k
end: Host
fn: probe () int
    Host()
    if: Out\a != 4 || Out\b != 5
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: probe
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: probe(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
